    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "I’ve always found math practical but not deeply intuitive. As an economics and chemistry enthusiast, I use it daily for problem-solving but struggle with abstract concepts. My parents’ mixed educational backgrounds—my dad had no formal schooling, my mom a bachelor’s—shaped my early math experiences. I appreciate its real-world applications but prefer concrete examples over theory.",
